===Etymology===
From {{inh-lite|gmw-cfr|gmh|min|mīn}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA-lite|gmw-cfr|/miː/|/mi/}}

===Determiner===
{{head-lite|gmw-cfr|determiners|masculine|menge|or|minge|feminine|meng|or|ming}}

# {{lb|gmw-cfr|Ripuarian}} [[my]] {{gloss-lite|first-person singular possessive}}
#: {{ux-lite|gmw-cfr|Wo hann ich dann '''mi''' Jlas henjestallt?|Where did I put '''my''' glass?}}

====Usage notes====
* The form {{m-lite|gmw-cfr||meng/ming}} is used for the neuter when strongly stressed: {{m-lite|gmw-cfr||Dat es ''ming'' Booch!|That's ''my'' book!}} Contrariwise, the form {{m-lite|gmw-cfr||mi}} may be used for the masculine and feminine when unstressed, chiefly with words for relatives: {{m-lite|gmw-cfr||mi Papp}} (“my father”, but less common than {{m-lite|gmw-cfr||menge Papp}}).

